      "firstSeenTime": 1777456786034,
      "lastSeenTime": 1777456786034,
      "summary": "Anchor elements (<a>) must have an `href` attribute to be recognized as a link.",
      "description": "**Cause:** \n The <a> (anchor) element does not have an `href` attribute. \n**Effect:** \nScreen readers on Windows will read the element as plain text without indicating it is a link. On Mac OS, VoiceOver will still read the anchor as a link, even if it's not. The element won't be included in the page's tab sequence by default, making it inaccessible using a keyboard. \n**Suggested Solutions:**\n* If the element should act as a link, add an `href` attribute that points to itself (<a href=\"#\">) \n* If the element is not meant to be a link, change it to something more appropriate, like a button",
      "tags": [
        {
          "id": "WCAG-4.1.2",
          "description": "4.1.2 Name, Role, Value  (Level A)",
          "link": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/name-role-value.html"
        },
        {
          "id": "WCAG-A"
        },
        {
          "id": "WCAG-undefined"
        },
        {
          "id": "WCAG2.0"
        }
      ],
      "knowledgeBaseLink": "https://knowledge.evinced.com/system-validations/anchor-without-href",
      "isNeedsReview": false,
      "isEvincedRecommended": true
    },
